cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bibliothecarius Modernus: an independent digital library of neglected Latin literature"
message: "If you use or cite an edition, cite the work, the edition year and its catalog id (plNNN-SSS), and the edition URL or DOI; each edition page offers BibTeX/RIS. Translations, essays and metadata are dedicated CC0 1.0; the project white paper (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18002473) is CC BY 4.0."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Wolfslayer
    given-names: Ryan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8914-9706"
    affiliation: Bibliothecarius Modernus (independent project)
repository-code: "https://github.com/bibliothecarius-modernus/bibliothecarius-modernus.github.io"
url: "https://bibliothecarius-modernus.github.io"
abstract: >-
  Bibliothecarius Modernus is an independent digital library of neglected Latin
  literature, publishing complete open translations, parallel texts, contextual
  research, audio and video editions, and machine-readable scholarly data — and,
  where the sources require it, new transcriptions from manuscripts. Editions are
  produced with AI models under a documented, curator-reviewed workflow (source
  integrity check, deterministic source-coverage validation, independent review
  by a second model family, recorded corrections, verified research record) and
  each edition states its source, method and review status. Latin sources are
  public domain (Migne, Patrologia Latina, or the named manuscript); the
  library's own contributions are CC0. Works range from the Apostolic Fathers to
  the medieval theologians, many lacking any prior English translation.
keywords:
  - digital library
  - Latin literature
  - patristics
  - medieval theology
  - Patrologia Latina
  - translation
  - open access
  - CC0
